{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226232-chain-of-command-question","id":1226232,"title":"Chain of Command Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-10T06:19:53-07:00","id":1226232,"title":"Chain of Command Question","content":"Since most uses of Dominate and its Devotions require Mesmirize to be already affecting them, does that, practically speaking, mean that you need to use Chain of Command twice for it to use anything but Mesmirize?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T20:18:30-07:00","id":1226653,"title":"","content":"fair points, I think thats an &quot;Ooops&quot; <br /> <br /> my own question is this.<br /> <br /> Is using the devotion as a boon on a mortal in the know, Member of Ashwood Abbey, etc etc, workable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T23:16:55-07:00","id":1226696,"title":"","content":"I would say that it's just an oversight. In my opinion, and the way I rule it, is that you don't need to apply it twice. Otherwise would be very uneffective and cumbersome. <br /> I guess the intention of Dev was to allow it to be used in dramatical situation: <br /> - the music starts, your friend turn his eyes on you and just a moment later you are shooting on xxx.<br /> <br /> - the pursuer reaches the prey but his eyes become empty: kill me and go to surrender to the police/my boss/whoever","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T23:36:16-07:00","id":1226701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1226232-chain-of-command-question#post1226232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since most uses of Dominate and its Devotions require Mesmirize to be already affecting them, does that, practically speaking, mean that you need to use Chain of Command twice for it to use anything but Mesmirize?</div> </div> </div> </div>To repeat from the Simple Question thread:<br /> <br /> It builds on Entombed Command and being able to use a proxy to deliver commands to a Mesmerized target is already a step up for EC's application to Mesmerize alone \u2014 it's a power that fills a hole in the systems Entombed Command allows you to create rather than a direct &quot;empower a herald to deal with anyone&quot; ability.<br /> <br /> tl;dr You need to have the subject able to be Mesmerized to use Chain of Command for anything other than Mesmerize, but the prerequisites of Chain of Command mean you have a lot more ways to render a subject Mesmerized than just Chain of Command.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}